# PLACEHOLDER -- Crimson Weed: the Warped Kush placeholder (itself Purple Kush's art, Warlon Mhite's,
# recoloured by a hue map) mapped onto the crimson forest's own colours, not redrawn. Warped teal
# foliage -> crimson roots' red (hue 340), the blue calyx -> weeping vines' deep red (hue 358), the
# violet accents -> crimson stem's brown-red; the orange pistils stay, as the weeping vines' tips
# and the crimson fungus have them. Every crop stage is flipped upside down, because the plant hangs
# from the canopy: the root (UPPER) wears stages 0-7 and the tip (LOWER) stages 8-11. The seed and
# the spliff's ember go red. Untinted, like Warped Kush: the models parent
# hempdustry:block/hanging_cross. Re-derive from warped_kush.mctex if that is ever redrawn.

